.page export 1 put variables into the environment of commands
.alias readonly

# SYNOPSIS
*export* [_NAME_[=_VALUE_]]...
*readonly* [_NAME_[=_VALUE_]]...

# DESCRIPTION
`export` is a gapsh builtin. It marks each _NAME_ so that programs started afterwards receive it in their environment, assigning _VALUE_ first if one is given. Without arguments it prints the exported variables in the form `export NAME="VALUE"`. `-n` is accepted and ignored.

`readonly` does exactly the same here: it exports, but it does not make a variable read-only.

# EXAMPLES
    export EDITOR=pnote
    export PATH="$PATH:/tmp/bin"

# SEE ALSO
unset(1), set(1), env(1), printenv(1)
